      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix Devin 1% usage inflating to 100%",
        "body": "The percentage normalization heuristic used `<= 1` to detect decimal fractions (0.12 → 12%), but the boundary value `1` represents integer 1% from the Devin API, not 100% as a decimal fraction. This caused CodexBar to show 100% used when actual daily/weekly usage was 1%.\r\n\r\nChanged `<= 1` to `< 1` in all four normalization sites in DevinUsageSnapshot.swift. Added a regression test for integer 1%.",
